::PC_U03_L03_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U03_L03_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.TR.9
Question:
Which statement correctly uses special triangle exact values?
{
=A. sin(pi/6)=1/2#Correct. pi/6 is 30 degrees, and sine is 1/2.
~B. sin(pi/6)=sqrt(3)/2#This is cos(pi/6), not sin(pi/6).
~C. tan(pi/4)=sqrt(2)/2#tan(pi/4)=1, not sqrt(2)/2.
~D. cos(pi/3)=sqrt(3)/2#cos(pi/3)=1/2, not sqrt(3)/2.
}
